    {
      "role": "candidate",
      "content": "When working with Prompt Engineering Fundamentals, the main focus was on designing and refining prompts to control AI outputs effectively. The biggest challenge wasn’t a single tool—it was the problem of ambiguity.\n\n🔑 Core Problem\nAI models are highly sensitive to phrasing. A vague or loosely structured prompt often leads to:\n\nUnclear or inconsistent answers\n\nOverly generic responses\n\nMissing context or incomplete reasoning\n\nThe fundamental issue was: How do we craft prompts that consistently yield accurate, relevant, and useful outputs?\n\n🛠️ Main Tools & Techniques\nInstead of one tool, it was a set of strategies:\n\nRole assignment → e.g., “Act as a data scientist…” to anchor the AI’s perspective.\n\nStep-by-step instructions → breaking tasks into smaller, logical steps.\n\nConstraints & formatting → specifying output style (tables, bullet points, LaTeX for math).\n\nIterative refinement → testing prompts, analyzing weaknesses, and adjusting wording.\n\nContext injection → feeding background info so the AI doesn’t guess.",
      "question_meta": null
    },
